      ],
      "sc:description": "MKado is a comprehensive Python toolkit designed for performing McDonald-Kreitman (MK) tests to analyze patterns of natural selection from aligned coding sequences. It implements both standard MK tests and various extensions, providing tools for estimating the fraction of adaptive substitutions ($\\alpha$).",
